<title>BELGIUM: EU agrees 1997/98 sugar supplies to remote islands.</title>
<headline>EU agrees 1997/98 sugar supplies to remote islands.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has agreed to ship 86,100 tonnes of subsidised sugar to the Canary Islands, Madeira, Azores and the Aegean islands in 1997/98 (July/June), European Commission officials said.</p>
<p>The Canary islands will receive 60,000 tonnes, unchanged from this season.</p>
<p>But Madeira and the Azores were only initially granted half their annual quotas of 10,000 tonnes and 6,500 tonnes respectively pending the provision of more data by Portugal. Madeira's quota is unchanged but Azores' is 1,000 tonnes higher.</p>
<p>The Aegean islands quota was split into two with an inner ring allocated 600 tonnes, down from 3,000 tonnes this season. An outer ring of islands will receive an unchanged 9,000 tonnes. -Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
